window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>I wanted to opt out.</p> <p>Instead, I matched with them.</p> <p>I’m not the perfect omega—not like my twin sister, who’s poised, polished, and basically made to be claimed by a top-tier pack. Me? I’d rather eat street corn in peace, start my own quilt shop, and avoid arrogant alphas with championship egos at all costs.</p> <p>But thanks to a glitch (or maybe a scheme), I end up matched with four celebrity Alphaball players who didn’t want an omega… and definitely weren’t expecting <a href=\"http://me.now/\">m</a>e. </p> <p>Now I’m stuck with four ridiculously attractive alphas who smell like they were made for me:</p> <p>Beck, the grumpy leader who thinks I’m a mistake.</p> <p>Kane, the smooth-talker with a hidden soft side.</p> <p>Rylan, the shameless flirt who gets under my skin.</p> <p>And Rio, the quiet one who just might see through my bullshit.</p> <p>They don’t want an omega. I don’t want a <a href=\"http://pack.so/\">p</a>ack.</p> <p>So why is my scent driving them all to the edge?</p> <p>*Knot So Perfect Omega is a standalone omegaverse. The characters do not shape shift. The main character has a pack and does not choose. Books in the Omega Match series can be listened to in any order.</p>"; 
